<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine tax office probes 300 grain, meat execs.</title>
<headline>Argentine tax office probes 300 grain, meat execs.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine courts are investigating more than 300 officials from 122 local grain and meat firms after the tax collection body DGI charged them with tax evasion, La Nacion daily said Thursday quoting official sources.</p>
<p>The companies, most of the medium and small size, were accused, among other charges, of falsifying documents and using &quot;ghost firms&quot; to do business.</p>
<p>La Nacion said grains and meat sector evade annually $1.3 billion in unpaid taxes.</p>
<p>((--Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
